env - run a command with an environment

SYNOPSIS
    env [-i] [name=value ...] [command [argument ...]]

DESCRIPTION
    With -i, start with an empty environment. Apply each assignment in
    order. With a command, run it using the resulting PATH. With no
    command, write each name=value pair.

EXAMPLES
    env LABEL="one two" printenv LABEL

SEE ALSO
    printenv(1), sh(1)
